<title>FRANCE: ADP Paris import traffic up 2.6pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>ADP Paris import traffic up 2.6pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 523,817 tonnes in 1996, an increase of 2.6 percent on 1995, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>Global 1996 ADP import traffic, by region, with percentage change on 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		   30,539 tonnes   down  9.2pct</p>
<p> European Union	   64,299 tonnes   up    12.0</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	    11,658 tonnes   up    8.9</p>
<p> North Africa		9,951 tonnes   down 14.8</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa     53,103 tonnes   up    8.3</p>
<p> North America	   181,603 tonnes   up    2.6</p>
<p> French territories     12,118 tonnes   down  6.7</p>
<p> Latin America	    19,043 tonnes   down  3.4</p>
<p> Middle East		24,792 tonnes   down  1.6</p>
<p> Far East		  116,713 tonnes   up    3.0</p>
<p> Total		     523,817 tonnes   up    2.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
